diffs.patch:
Index: openwiki/.claims/gatekeepers/contract.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/gatekeepers/contract.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/gatekeepers/contract.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,148 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:4f2421a1ee3c8399b4b487b0dd39e8545c6d3b06485a32d6a4307836017ef6ad",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0415800acf7b46fb9a3521effd1841ac",
+      "statement": "GatekeeperVendor exposes describe (with providesAuth/autoProvisionsAccount flags), connectAccount (whose returned OAuth URL must carry a cryptographic nonce to prevent replay), getSupportedResources (empty hides the vendor), getTypeScriptTypes (the agent type database source), and optional createAccount present only when autoProvisionsAccount is declared — which only creates accounts, takes no user identity, and is gated on the declaration flag rather than stub probing; scopes select \"full\" or transient \"auth\", and resourceUrlPatterns semantics are omitted=all versus []=none, which vendors must not conflate.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L445-L523",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dfbeea78dbfd5d984823674b587e1758ffa0a5273abce173e6d04989a1be1a6f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_720393e1d3214767bb87171f6a818eb9",
+      "statement": "GatekeeperConnectCallback.complete's expiresAt means when credentials stop being refreshable (not a transparently-refreshable token's cache expiry) so the UI can proactively show expiry; credentialsExpired is called once on revocation detection and credentialsRestored after reconnect.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L525-L556",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d1cb02b991a2eb997daeda85916dadcf437b9fc9ce9b0e8c3f022cea576a7e98:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a3a48aa1ed1045f8ad7b3a02ef9f8de8",
+      "statement": "GatekeeperUser is the privileged per-user adapter whose capability represents access to all of the user's data through the vendor — only the Workshop should hold it; getGatekeeperClassFor returns a DO class imbued via ctx.props with the user's credentials and resource id, and the overseer calls it before permissions are granted, with permissions requested afterwards via setPermissions on the instantiated gatekeeper.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L558-L593",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ce5e10643cbe1255b6a71c7a6cd39bafbe7fb9fb3ae35bbb3029d709be1ee3dc:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_de054ac0d0044094a706f753f27ff7f5",
+      "statement": "getAuthenticatedEmail must return a provider-verified email (Google email_verified, GitHub primary+verified, Cloudflare account email) because the Workshop keys accounts by email and an unverified address would allow account takeover.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L621-L628",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b2a7506b9502700ae296e48f23b96fec3189f0769e686883916742057d68cb48:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_5ff2f57ecd9b4645bee510bea26a8d0f",
+      "statement": "Singleton/management-UI methods on GatekeeperUser exist only on auto-provisioned accounts whose describe declares them (Workshop gates on declaration flags), and GatekeeperUserVerifier is an opaque capability passed back only to the gatekeeper that created it, which may call a public-but-non-standard method on it because the runtime cannot yet unwrap a Fetcher's props.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L644-L668",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9c4c6108a6663c7046a59cc57c845409609d48bc18794d780173251145536e4c:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L674-L689",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:eea24f524722e3f1b96f6c0c1b8f6eaa94201293b6aaf10716f6d17ea5cd7f78:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_02ee3a4145be42819f50b6c4be3cd67c",
+      "statement": "A Gatekeeper instance runs as a Durable Object Facet child of the overseer, exposed only to the overseer; its startSession hands the gadget a session where every operation must go through the approval queue — observations authorized before data returns and side-effecting actions not executed until approved — with simulation of unapproved actions suggested (author's choice), getAutoApprovableActions describing only the potential action-kind set, and getAgentCatalog access itself an authorized observation.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L691-L751",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:728456b20c36be9e5dd6cff9144e2cecaab2ffb08edc621cae2dff3af8f5bd4b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_adbc914a586f4479ba4c4f59e9e29933",
+      "statement": "addObserver must verify a new observer may see everything previously observed through the gatekeeper (throwing otherwise), re-run verification on repeat calls to catch upstream revocation, and mark future observations that must hide from someone with excludeObservers; most gatekeepers only check general read access, while broad singletons may log actual observations; removeObserver is idempotent.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L753-L795",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4647a324684782e5d5bf8181f1322d696154438a5d2a545bf34f04b636812d5b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_83bab1526c8244e1ac60a0b0b7f7ff52",
+      "statement": "The overseer applies queued actions via applyAction/rejectAction/revertAction keyed by sequential action id; a gatekeeper must always submit actions for approval (no mode skips the check); rejectAction may request a gadget restart when simulation state can't roll back, and revertAction is optional but expected, returning message/canRetry/restart semantics.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L800-L853",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:09382b9a6071c8382803f849e299e671c51954129fc0790a9e72e02112eb8ae2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0d9eb594449946deb36b7cbeffa4539c",
+      "statement": "ObservationAuthorizer.authorizeObservation must be called on every read and awaited before returning data (may be called after fetching, before returning, so the description can describe actual data); ApprovalQueue extends it with submitAction, which resolves quickly while the action may be applied much later, with the action id returned to applyAction/rejectAction.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L855-L869",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a94e63566e34e63a68c5b90484e7643f4b1f88e7338635e3d7fbb6de7286e323:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L928-L957",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d0b1fee60f466e4ce26b904d3cb76024034e8c85eb12b810016de1885606b083:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7e9317ba46924c07987c535947f3025c",
+      "statement": "ActionDescription carries display title/description, implementsRevert, the awaitDecision hint (set when effects are not simulated so the agent harness suspends the turn instead of working against unapplied state), and the per-action autoApprovable author verdict (absent means never auto-approvable even with a matching rule); ActionKind pairs a stable machine tag with a display label and policy keys on the tag.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L1104-L1124",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fa4ca49e395b6ddee9aa72a36a6dbf71efd474d2bb21b3b2a87006dbc91d7297:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d23eaa36d94747e9963238631401a0a6",
+      "statement": "The workshop-side auto-approval drain applies eligible pending actions in id order under a per-gatekeeper single-flight guard; eligibility requires both the gatekeeper author's autoApprovable verdict and a user-enabled rule for the action's tag, the approval is attributed to the rule's enabler (running under their authority), and the drain stops at the first manual gate or apply failure without ever skipping ahead.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/auto-approval.ts#L1-L99",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:14577b3411a779ee70f5a4dbe8d82946fd095b33607d9315ca57801aedae9df0:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b421ec4cf2f4421ea60be707d5d57365",
+      "statement": "bindHook registers a persistent callback the gatekeeper must not store itself — the callback is tied to the session behind the ApprovalQueue, and later HookInitiator.startHook opens a new session returning a fresh callback plus queue; hooks start disabled with HookController.enable invoked only after user approval, and persistent stubs are built with the [restore](params)+ctx.restore(params) pattern so they can be stored and re-created deterministically.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L959-L1047",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ff99860670958e949bcc0d566cd67d1deff753211ba1adc5e106637138c76752:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_17ec138d763840a4be0ca98308b37841",
+      "statement": "HookController.enable(initiator, target) replaces any prior initiator, HookTargetMetadata is display/routing only (never authorization or identity), and on delivery the gatekeeper must call startHook() first, authorize the observation on the returned queue, then invoke the callback.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L1240-L1282",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:13e0e31b01dfcb9dffffa8e554b779f4ec67c5ab52976854b6a904936b056d59:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-01T04:46:04.795Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/gatekeepers/lifecycle.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/gatekeepers/lifecycle.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/gatekeepers/lifecycle.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:4fbe499e2274bd42f2f1ffa78ab341ede8022f604e2caac90a5eb2ab4d3bcce1",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9245ed636978463aa118ebf7fa8c1394",
+      "statement": "UserDurableObject.connectAccount resolves the GATEKEEPER_* vendor binding, refuses if the deployment's admin config disabled that gatekeeper, allocates the next account id, mints a GatekeeperConnectCallbackImpl entrypoint carrying {userId, accountId, vendorId} props, and returns the vendor's OAuth popup URL.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/user.ts#L1142-L1167",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8905a2f14807872f8ee97dcbef7e97b2f8a1fceed33e92ffe00a465e8eb3fc4a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9bb113f53505433dbac7f6c4c38888f1",
+      "statement": "On OAuth completion the gatekeeper invokes the callback's complete(account, expiresAt?), which persists the account record (id, account stub, description, vendorId, expected credential expiry) via putConnectedAccount, while credentialsExpired/credentialsRestored flip the record's expiry flags so the UI can prompt reconnect.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/user.ts#L1734-L1760",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:63e6fb57efb553d5d31d340aa356e697761d00698096a802897e17aabe3243ff:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ee8551da15cb4f839ecbc89af757e8d5",
+      "statement": "Connected-account listing skips records that fail to deserialize (e.g. a stub pointing at a gatekeeper no longer bound in the deployment) so one stale account cannot break listing, provisioning, or opt-in for the others.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/user.ts#L1169-L1188",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3f53b138401518e067e16719a566e79e2b4d3ca67a6a812cd5121feee5681eb2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b593f91ec828491ca0ba832b561e51ed",
+      "statement": "Disconnecting calls the account's revoke() (the gatekeeper's cleanup hook for its own per-user storage, best-effort for opt-in ambient accounts so a throwing gatekeeper never blocks disconnect) then deletes the record, clearing Cloudflare billing state too; a forced (\"enabled\") ambient account cannot be disconnected by the user; reconnectAccount delegates to the account's nonce-protected reconnect URL keeping all bindings working.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/user.ts#L1500-L1560",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:84a9d9fd9ac9330882411dc04592d8826cfd087790d21a2cc49ae52c4082d946:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_4e0a97bcb62745c3a1ca33ef0b731256",
+      "statement": "Ambient gatekeeper provisioning uses a per-vendor three-state mode stored in AdminConfig.ambientGatekeeperModes and resolved by provisioning-policy.ts as the single chokepoint: disabled (nothing provisioned, existing dormant), optional (user opt-in from Connectors — the default, so ambient authority is never imposed without an admin opting in), and enabled (auto-provisioned for every user, forced and not user-removable).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/provisioning-policy.ts#L1-L34",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6dc39bd007588ac28493f07843e20e1a3e773d7c0474e62d4429c1daa7493473:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2e86e1bb3a6d4451bb0190f78a9ecca5",
+      "statement": "GatekeeperVendor.createAccount mints a connected account with no OAuth flow and takes no user identity — safe on the public interface because it only creates accounts and cannot look up or return existing ones; the Workshop persists the returned account like any connected account and treats it as the authority thereafter, resolving the description before allocating the id so a describe failure doesn't burn a slot.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/user.ts#L1255-L1267",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:acf32a23e51ca6a1f7b20edb532479267d75cdac41f745b95ed4001ef9f9efa7:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-shared/src/gatekeeper.ts#L514-L522",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2c01756dc2b95fd16712cfd5016a793d021878f77e31204b28e8c898c6163f3d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_beb196e3a284487cb3614ca396ab0f90",
+      "statement": "Auto-provisioning is idempotent and best-effort per vendor (one failing vendor never blocks the others), creates at most one account per vendor, and is deduped against concurrent calls via a shared promise because the loop's cross-worker RPCs release the DO input gate and overlapping calls could otherwise mint duplicates; only \"enabled\" vendors are forced, \"optional\" vendors are added on demand.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/user.ts#L1291-L1329",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a822f948cb20a523252d25d05b648005e0b819ee611337da79091b13bca44ce2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_74e28460743c44c7b44257e4b64b6b49",
+      "statement": "Only Cloudflare persists a grant during sign-in: linkConnectedAccountFromLogin treats a repeated sign-in as re-authorization, revoking the stale gatekeeper-side grant and pointing the existing record (same id, stable UI references) at the fresh grant so billing doesn't break when the old token expired; the grant covers billing only, with gadget-facing resources authorized separately later.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/user.ts#L1552-L1600",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7c5cf77ae6e5eb15cc2ff4e8326d97cbf5117f9a95adccf79eeabcababd15839:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_31839b3568ba4459a2cd8368e58e43fa",
+      "statement": "getGatekeeperClassFor is the single core-side chokepoint where a resourceUrl becomes a capability (reached only via user/UI-facing Overseer.newGatekeeper and blueprint instantiation, never gadget or agent code), and it blocks whole disabled gatekeepers and individually disabled resources (AdminConfig.disabledResources keyed by vendor with disabled urlPatterns) so a request bypassing the separately filtered picker/agent listings still cannot mint the capability.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/user.ts#L1666-L1691",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:54e93c0b070abfe8a4c81d6fb9c91073172cc5f94979c5b867ed08c712aff52f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_378988ca9a634db69312059dec9b3f27",
+      "statement": "Ambient modes also gate surfacing: listAddableGatekeepers offers only \"optional\" vendors the user hasn't added (backs the Connectors Available section), and listProvidedAccounts hides disabled-mode singletons while keeping their data dormant for later re-enablement.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/user.ts#L1217-L1229",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:33bd82d332cec77352c698601a8a9eee75a7a70a134a6ca63df3ed26e09726ba:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/src/user.ts#L1330-L1347",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d7d89a11de98b14de64f9aa64c289a2ef73a911c89c2d29260caaf3675439a40:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-01T04:46:04.795Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/operations/testing.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/operations/testing.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/operations/testing.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,98 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:fd5c362541a92a1f41bf92fdcc000031223dba8cdb4bcfba3a067e6da5530ae4",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_07801bdda3384be9a15a7f483448d507",
+      "statement": "Each package's test run is a Vite+ task (not a script) so vitest scratch paths (node_modules/.vite, .vite-temp, .wrangler — excluded workspace-wide because wrangler scratch reaches past the owning package) stay out of the fingerprint; the cached vp path replays instantly for untouched packages but loses to plain vitest (test:run) on a just-edited package by more than the whole suite costs on a small one.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://scripts/vitest-task-vite-config.ts#L13-L34",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2895f0403ce6bb2c73371be823a4650604e9ec7a44c4d7e0dfc7241d67e158d5:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://scripts/vitest-task-vite-config.ts#L63-L72",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9363e20776c08a768a596fecb90b5f73e51a1abc2509d6c80637a803373b3c60:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7456deca1b5f4989a9b26990cccce3d2",
+      "statement": "Every test command is wrapped in the shared watchdog (idle 60s / total 600s) which kills the whole process tree and exits 124; command arrays are cached as one entry per command so codegen ahead of tests can replay while tests re-run, and the thresholds are baked into the command string because a cached vp run strips undeclared env vars.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://scripts/vitest-task-vite-config.ts#L76-L108",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e39b5c6fc16f981a8c4ee41a57b3bc8f1a6a12da3f51787c453395ede7fa88ba:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9eb7a494eb3d4551bbf8f41f3efa3a7c",
+      "statement": "The watchdog exists because nothing else bounds a wedged run: vitest's timeouts are enforced inside the test worker that died, Vite+ has no task timeout, and vitest-pool-workers imports Miniflare without onWorkerdCrashRestart so a dead workerd leaves the pool awaiting a reply that never arrives; silence (not wall clock) is the primary detector since a healthy vitest run prints a line per completed file.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://scripts/with-timeout.ts#L1-L28",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48af54997541dc3211f3ebe5ac0153fb0889ffcf4d0b774fee4dc6ff4ec9cac7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7fe99e72ee7c47b5b00059ac0154b77c",
+      "statement": "Packages whose tests run in workerd (router, typed-storage, backend-utils, workshop-backend, gatekeeper-scheduler) load assert-workerd.ts as a setup file, which throws unless navigator.userAgent is Cloudflare-Workers — so a vitest-pool-workers pool that fails to start fails the suite instead of silently falling back to Node, which would look like a pass in packages importing no cloudflare:* module.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://scripts/assert-workerd.ts#L1-L14",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8fe6a102011693e5c4634c423abdd4eb0c4324cc356307edd9e2d0629e7725bf:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d781c8d900bf433c99b15f4f5a2360e1",
+      "statement": "workshop-backend's unit suite runs inside workerd to exercise production runtime APIs (e.g. Uint8Array.toHex/fromBase64 and crypto.subtle used by the sharing module), binding a test-only SQLite DO TEST_OVERSEER for the Overseer cost-persistence integration test without loading the full deployment configuration.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/vitest.config.ts#L1-L30",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3887b601282da7a700f63b35e0e0b996ac8b35bc0d195c00780365f488b5f0f0:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c5d21296654041adb8a11f63c8e718d3",
+      "statement": "The integration suite boots the real wrangler.jsonc configuration with remoteBindings:false, pays workerd's cold start with a 60s first-test timeout, and filters only the exact unhandled rejections its reset-recovery tests provoke (expected open-error codes, abortAllDurableObjects, injected user-DO resets) while leaving all other unhandled errors fatal.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://packages/workshop-backend/vitest.integration.config.ts#L1-L46",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b13c14e94a8dbda9373699ac0a87570c271f00d8242280977605843740913f9:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_81273155e4244077a248bdaced91166c",
+      "statement": "The integration harness boots the real workshop-backend alongside parameterized real gatekeepers under wrangler's createTestHarness, reading each package's checked-in wrangler.jsonc with build.cwd pinned and main absolutized for generated-main workers, so a suite for a new gatekeeper is a new handler module rather than a fork; it also defines the TEST vendor id derived from the binding suffix and an admin username mirroring run-dev-server.",
+      "evidence": [
